# Translation API Fallback & Resilience Specification

## Executive Summary
This document outlines the technical specification, setup instructions, architecture design, and production code implementation for an ultra-resilient Python translation bot. It resolves API rate limits and character quotas using a multi-provider fallback strategy, persistent TTL caching, per-user rate limiting, exponential backoff retries, and localized response handling tailored for Discord bot environments.

---

## 1. System Architecture Diagram

```text
[ User Request (Discord Message) ]
                │
                ▼
    [ Input Validation & Truncation ] ──(Exceeds 1900 Chars)──► Return Length Warning
                │
             (Valid)
                │
                ▼
        [ Cache Layer (Diskcache) ] ──(Hit)──► Return Cached Translation
                │
             (Miss)
                │
                ▼
   [ Fallback Translation Pipeline ]
        ├── Step 1: GoogleTranslator (deep-translator) + Retries
        ├── Step 2: Puter REST API Endpoint / Bridge + Timeout
        ├── Step 3: DeepL SDK (Official API Key) + Format Mapping
        └── Step 4: Fallback Localized Warning Response
```
## 2. Key Features
Async & Non-Blocking: Runs synchronous translation libraries inside thread pool executors via asyncio.

Dynamic Failover Chain: Automatically fails over across Google, Puter, and DeepL.

Retry Logic with Exponential Backoff: Handles transient network blips per provider before escalating down the pipeline.

Persistent TTL Caching: Retains translations for 7 days via diskcache to save redundant quota usage.

Per-User Rate Limiting: Enforces cooldowns to protect the bot infrastructure against user spam.

Input Sanitization: Truncates and validates input strings to fit Discord’s 2,000-character message limit.

Localization (i18n): Decouples user-facing responses from error logging to support multi-language bot deployments.

